          <item>Use the Comparison Theorem with $$f(x) = 1 \slash x^{2}$$ to show that $${\int_{1}^{\infty}{g(x)}}dx$$ is convergent.</item>
          <item>Illustrate part (b) by graphing $$f$$ and $$g$$ on the same screen for $$1 \leqslant x \leqslant 10$$ . Use your graph to explain intuitively why $${\int_{1}^{\infty}{g(x)}}dx$$ is convergent.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <cell header="true">$$t$$</cell>
              <cell header="true">$$\int_{1}^{t}{\lbrack(\sin^{2}x) \slash x^{2}\rbrack dx}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>2</cell>
              <cell>0.447453</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>5</cell>
              <cell>0.577101</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>10</cell>
              <cell>0.621306</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>100</cell>
              <cell>0.668479</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>1,000</cell>
              <cell>0.672957</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>10,000</cell>
              <cell>0.673407</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <paragraph>It appears that the integral is convergent.</paragraph>
      </solution>
